From: Proton CRM <noreply@proton.local>
Subject: [PATCH] P6 C1 fix: the agent availability-status selector

Gives agents the control the handbook describes and the P6 review found
missing: a "My status" page where an agent picks Available / Lunch / Break /
Toilet / Prayer / Coaching / Training, plus (for `workforce.manage` holders
only) the catalogue editor that makes §4.17's "an administrator can add a
status without a software release" reachable from the product instead of
from a hand-written Firestore document.

Backs features/routing/status_router.py's four endpoints. Nav visibility is
gated on `presence.set_own_status` exactly the way 0039/0041/0053 gate theirs
on their own permission; the backend's require_permission remains the actual
boundary.

WHY THIS IS A PAGE AND NOT CHATWOOT'S TOP-BAR AVAILABILITY CONTROL. That
control writes Chatwoot's own fixed three-value enum (online/busy/offline),
which has no extension point -- extending it would mean patching upstream
components this sandbox cannot even read (see the note below), and it would
still have to mirror into the same three values. So the named statuses live
on their own page and MIRROR: picking Lunch sets your real Chatwoot
availability to Busy and records "lunch" alongside it. The top bar keeps
working, unmodified, and keeps showing Busy -- which is also why routing
still excludes you correctly when the custom-status service is down.

After-Call Work and Offline are not offered in the picker (the backend
refuses them too): ACW is entered automatically at call end and times out on
its own, and Offline belongs to Chatwoot's control. The page reads the
backend's `system_managed` flag rather than hard-coding that list.

NOTE: hand-constructed, and NOT verified with `git apply --check` against a
real checkout -- this sandbox has no network access to clone upstream or the
fork, the same constraint recorded for patch 0053. The three anchored hunks
below apply ON TOP OF 0053: their context lines are transcribed verbatim from
0053's own added lines (the workforce API helper, the Workforce nav entry and
the proton/workforce route), which is what `git apply`'s offset search relies
on, and the line numbers assume 0053 has been applied and nothing else has
touched these three files since. Hunk arithmetic was script-generated and the
patch applies cleanly to a synthetic tree reconstructing that context -- that
proves internal consistency only. Verify on the first Cloud Build before
demoing the page; it is a row in
docs/analysis/2026-08-09-blocked-work-register.md beside 0053's.
